The 92-glyph ASCII sample font supplied with the KITAQ manuals is
original work by DAISUKE OBA. The author confirmed original authorship and
permission to publish it under MIT on 2026-09-12.

Copyright (c) 2026 DAISUKE OBA

This covers examples/beginner_samples/assets/ascii.c in the development
workspace, samples/assets/ascii.c in the manual distribution, and its
format conversions, including samples/font_gb.h and samples/font.chr.
The full font MIT notice is in licenses/fonts/ASCII-font-MIT.txt in this
distribution. Preserve it when redistributing these glyphs or conversions.

This permission concerns the supplied sample glyphs. It does not grant
rights in other fonts supplied by users, loaded from ROMs, or present in
screenshots or analysis inputs and outputs.

KOKURA's egui GUI uses fonts from epaint_default_fonts 0.32.3:

- Hack: Copyright 2018 Source Foundry Authors, MIT; its DejaVu and
  Bitstream Vera heritage has additional notices, including the Bitstream
  Vera License. See licenses/fonts/epaint_default_fonts-0.32.3/Hack-Regular.txt.
- Noto Emoji: SIL Open Font License 1.1. See the same directory's OFL.txt.
- Ubuntu Light: Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0. See the same directory's UFL.txt.
- emoji-icon-font: Copyright (c) 2014 John Slegers, MIT. See the same
  directory's emoji-icon-font-mit-license.txt.

The same directory includes font-copyright-records.txt transcribed from
the shipped Noto Emoji and Ubuntu Light font metadata.
Preserve applicable font notices when packaging
the GUI, including when font bytes are embedded in the executable.

The SDL GUI uses font8x8 0.3.1. Its Rust implementation is MIT, Copyright
(c) 2017 Joaquin Rosales. Upstream identifies its bitmap glyphs as public
domain and records their provenance. Full original LICENSE and README.md
are preserved in licenses/fonts/font8x8-0.3.1/.

The SDL GUI also searches for locally installed Windows fonts. These
system fonts retain their own terms; loading them does not grant
permission to redistribute them. KOKURA's MIT license does not relicense
any third-party font.

These notices identify font rights separately from the project code.
They do not replace third-party licenses or add restrictions to code
covered by the MIT License above.
